      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "One of the problems with this is that dynamic bones (especially with colliders) is far, far worse than draw calls off materials/meshes. Ranking with a heavy weight on dynamic bones is a big deal because dynamic bones is the single biggest thing under our control as players to reduce lag. Things like IK, positional sound, and networking are lag-causers we can't fix on avatars. Dynamic bones, materials, meshes, we can. Of those things, dynamic bones is up with IK in performance loss. Draw calls is bad, yeah, but ultimately an avatar with 1 draw call and 40 dynamic bones with colliders in their body/hands will be far worse for your performance than an avatar with 20 materials and no dynamic bones.\n\nI like the ability to see the rank of your avatar, but being able to see others' ranks seems to be the problem here. Instead of scrapping an effective ranking system that actually weighs appropriately what matters, just hide it from the public so it's creators shaming themselves instead of players shaming players.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
