      "value": "@{5bbbf6aa17bab877dd8bc723|full_name}: collision is nothing more then a bunch of math based on positions. even if not actually interacting it's still calculating where the colliders would be relative to each bone, and if they happen to be interacting or not. so even if 'idle' they still have a significant amount of calculations going on. (i know. late response, but atleast you got one, right?)",
