  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "tl;dr: The ranking system should instead be set on a sliding scale based on Draw Calls, with these avatar details still available to see.   \n\nWhile I love the spirit of the new avatar ranking and how its trying to be helpful, the community has been pretty loudly complaining that it is not doing its job and instead just causing a lot of unjustified toxic behavior. I won’t completely go into all of the details since nearly every post is saying the same thing, but I will agree that it's incredibly agitating thinking that models with 16 materials and meshes will think they are justified in not texture atlasing because their avatar will be ranked the same as an avatar done by professional game artists that only have a single mesh and material, simply because that model has a single dynamic bone collider.\n\nIt would make better sense if the ranking system was able to have a setting to turn on draw call viewing and give you a real number so you can actually tell who is the cause of lag, then that person would be able to open up their details and see what is taking up all the draw calls. You could then still have green-yellow-orange-red dots to show the average draw calls being taken up, though honestly I don’t see a reason why to have it always by the nametag. Having any sort of marking always visible will cause people to have a class mentality and cause toxicity. Instead I would say just have it in the user menus, that way if someone is searching out for the person giving them lag, they have the means to without needing to openly advertise to people that have beasts of computers and aren’t interested in that sort of thing. \n\nAgain, I thank VRChat for trying to be helpful and looking out for people that are always suffering from low fps, but with how it is right now, it’s going to be more damaging than helpful, and needs a serious rework.",
